       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day. Single doses are usually capped at 800 mg. This order is double the daily maximum, and each dose is double the usual single-dose limit.\n- **Risks:** At this level, the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours:** the typical range for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg per day in total:** for example, 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please tell me the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
